== Temple lower bound for E1 with beta = CI-k E2 (upper bound on E2, wrong direction) ==
   Temple needs beta <= E2. Any certified beta is a lower bound on E2: the same kind of
   statement as the gap itself. 'false' = the computed 'bound' exceeds the true E1.
beta = CI E2: 3/88 'bounds' false; beta = exact E2: 0 false (theorem)
   false: plaq1 g2=0.5 k=2 'E1 >=' -0.364038 but E1 = -1.666966
   false: plaq1 g2=0.5 k=3 'E1 >=' -1.611476 but E1 = -1.666966
   false: ladder2 g2=0.5 k=2 'E1 >=' -6.777975 but E1 = -7.396889

